om1gss\", \"sessionID\": \"ses_f88fc143affeX5td08cX1wEVEv\"}, {\"id\": \"prt_0771530ba001do6hvYMEXjLgOS\", \"tool\": \"vteam_group_post\", \"type\": \"tool\", \"state\": {\"time\": {\"end\": 1788704273956, \"start\": 1788704273910}, \"input\": {\"teamId\": \"tm_0000000001\", \"content\": \"任务已创建：测试vteam会话功能（t_0000000001）。\\n\\n任务计划：\\n1. 产品经理-1：探索vteam会话功能结构，输出模块功能清单\\n2. 测试-1：基于功能清单编写测试用例\\n3. 测试-1：执行测试用例，产出测试报告和结论\\n\\n测试地址：http://web:3000\\n账号密码：admin/admin123\\n\\n请各成员准备就绪，任务启动后立即开始工作。\", \"selfInstanceId\": \"tmm_0000000002\"}, \"title\": \"\", \"output\": \"{\\\"messageId\\\":\\\"m_0000000039\\\",\\\"channelId\\\":\\\"c_0000000003\\\",\\\"attachment\\\":null}\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"metadata\": {\"truncated\": false}}, \"callID\": \"call_3ee597985856423f96ce2c12\", \"messageID\": \"msg_07714c83b001PIOh1w8tom1gss\", \"sessionID\": \"ses_f88fc143affeX5td08cX1wEVEv\"}, {\"id\": \"prt_07715362d001aP6ys3loP7n31L\", \"cost\": 0, \"type\": \"step-finish\", \"reason\": \"tool-calls\", \"tokens\": {\"cache\": {\"read\": 44288, \"write\": 0}, \"input\": 839, \"total\": 45540, \"output\": 413, \"reasoning\": 0}, \"messageID\": \"msg_07714c83b001PIOh1w8tom1gss\", \"sessionID\": \"ses_f88fc143affeX5td08cX1wEVEv\"}, {\"id\": \"prt_07715661c0012sWMx89MzZIGYx\", \"type\": \"step-start\", \"messageID\": \"msg_077153642001557PaZGwh9D2Ew\", \"sessionID\": \"ses_f88fc143affeX5td08cX1wEVEv\"}, {\"id\": \"prt_07715661f001tHLt5kqcwyHkZH\", \"text\": \"OK, so group_post works with tmm_ prefix. The issue is that issue_create, task_transition, and other task-scoped tools require the worker to have a bound session for the task. Since I\'m in team direct chat context, I can use group_post and notify_agent (with tmm_ prefix) but not task-scoped tools like issue_create, task_transition, etc.\\n\\nLet me think about what I can do:\\n1. I can use group_post to communicate with the team\\n2. I can use notify_agent to send messages to team members\\n3. I cannot use issue_create, task_transition, etc. because the task sessions aren\'t bound\\n\\nBut wait - the user wants me to organize the work. I need to create issues and assign them. But I can\'t do that from team direct chat context.\\n\\nMaybe I should use notify_agent to ask team members to start working. The notify_agent with tmm_ prefix might work.\\n\\nLet me try notify_agent to reach the product manager and tester.\\n\\nActually, looking at the system prompt again for notify_agent: \\\"参数 {taskId, selfInstanceId, targetInstanceId, content}\\\" - it needs taskId. But the task was created and I have the taskId (t_0000000001). Let me try.\\n\\nBut wait - notify_agent also needs the worker to have a bound session? Let me check the error pattern.\\n\\nActually, let me re-read: \\\"调用 vteam MCP 工具时，落库类工具（group_post / notify_agent / submit_artifact）的selfInstanceId 参数必须填写你的任务实例 id（ta_ 前缀）\\\"\\n\\nBut group_post worked with tmm_ prefix. So maybe notify_agent will also work with tmm_ prefix?\\n\\nLet me try notify_agent to reach the product manager. The product manager\'s team-level instance is tmm_0000000001. But the task-level instance is ta_0000000003.\\n\\nLet me try with tmm_ prefix for selfInstanceId and targetInstanceId.\\n\\nActually, I think the issue is more fundamental. The task was created but the worker process isn\'t bound to any task instance. The task instances exist in the database but no worker session is active for them.\\n\\nLet me try a different approach. Since I can use group_post, let me announce the task and the plan to the team. Then I\'ll ask the team members to start working. The product manager and tester can then create issues themselves or start working.\\n\\nActually, let me try notify_agent with tmm_ prefix.\", \"time\": {\"end\": 1788704318027, \"start\": 1788704286239}, \"type\": \"reasoning\", \"messageID\": \"msg_077153642001557PaZGwh9D2Ew\", \"sessionID\": \"ses_f88fc143affeX5td08cX1wEVEv\"}, {\"id\": \"prt_07715e24c0010op3F83vXZpLx8\", \"tool\": \"vteam_notif